verses.display_text:
Blessed is the man who did not walk in the counsel of the ungodly,
and did not stand in the way of sinners,
and did not sit in the seat of pestilent men;

announcing the Lord’s decree:
The Lord said to me, ‘You are My son;
today I have begotten you.

Rise, Lord! Save me, my God!
For Thou didst strike all who were my enemies without cause;
Thou didst crush sinners’ teeth.

For there is no truth in their mouth;
their heart is vain.
Their throat is an open tomb;
with their tongues they practiced deceit.

Let all who hope in Thee rejoice;
they will exult for ever, and Thou wilt dwell among them.
All who love Thy name will boast in Thee.

I grew weary with my groaning;
every night I will bathe my bed,
with my tears I will wet my resting place.

Rise, Lord, in Thine anger;
be exalted within the boundaries of my enemies.
Awake, Lord my God, in the ordinance which Thou didst command,

Have mercy on me, Lord;
see my humiliation from my enemies,
Thou who raisest me from the gates of death,

so that I may proclaim all Thy praises
in the gates of daughter Zion;
I will exult in Thy salvation.

The Lord is known as He executes judgments;
the sinner was caught in the works of his own hands.
A song of Diapsalma.

Appoint a lawgiver over them, Lord;
let nations know that they are human beings.
Diapsalma.

The sinner provoked the Lord.
According to the abundance of his anger, he will not seek out;
God is not before him.

His ways are profaned at every time;
Thy judgments are removed from before him;
he will lord it over all his enemies.

He sits in ambush with rich people,
to kill an innocent person in hiding places;
his eyes look toward the needy.

He lurks in hiding like a lion in its enclosure;
he lurks to seize a poor man,
to seize a poor man as he drags him away.

For behold, sinners bent a bow;
they prepared arrows for a quiver,
to shoot down in the moonless dark the upright in heart.

The Lord is in His holy temple;
the Lord’s throne is in heaven.
His eyes look toward the needy;
His eyelids examine the sons of men.

All turned aside; together they became useless;
there is no one who shows kindness, not even one.
Their throat is an open tomb;
with their tongues they practiced deceit.
The venom of asps is under their lips;
their mouth is full of cursing and bitterness.
Their feet are swift to shed blood;
brokenness and misery are in their ways,
and they did not know a way of peace.
There is no fear of God before their eyes.

One who acts wickedly is held in contempt before him,
but he honors those who fear the Lord;
one who swears to his neighbor and does not set it aside.

Thou madest known to me ways of life;
Thou wilt fill me with gladness in Thy presence;
pleasures are at Thy right hand for ever.

A prayer of David.
Hear my righteousness, Lord;
attend to my petition;
give ear to my prayer, not from deceitful lips.

Arise, Lord; get ahead of them and trip them up;
rescue my soul from an ungodly man,
Thy sword from the enemies of Thy hand.

The Lord is my firm foundation, my refuge, and my rescuer;
my God is my helper, and I will hope in Him;
my protector, the horn of my salvation, my supporter.

And the earth was shaken and began to tremble;
the foundations of the mountains were troubled
and shaken because God was angry with them.

Smoke rose in His anger,
and fire from His face set things ablaze;
coals were kindled from Him.

And He made darkness His hiding place;
His tent was around Him,
dark water in clouds of the air.

My God’s way is blameless;
the Lord’s sayings are tried by fire;
He is a protector of all who hope in Him.

Thou wilt rescue me from the people’s disputes;
Thou wilt appoint me head of nations;
a people I did not know served me.

my rescuer from my wrathful enemies.
Thou wilt raise me above those who rise against me;
Thou wilt rescue me from an unjust man.

His going out is from heaven’s edge,
and his arrival reaches heaven’s edge;
there is no one who will be hidden from his heat.

And spare Thy servant from others;
if they do not rule over me, then I will be blameless
and cleansed from great sin.

Now I know that the Lord saved His anointed;
He will hear him from His holy heaven;
in mighty acts is the salvation of His right hand.

You will make them like a fiery furnace at the time of your presence;
the Lord in His anger will throw them into turmoil,
and fire will devour them.

My strength dried up like a potsherd;
my tongue is stuck to my throat,
and Thou broughtest me down into the dust of death.

For many dogs surrounded me;
a gathering of evildoers encompassed me;
they dug into my hands and feet.

The needy will eat and be filled,
and those who seek the Lord will praise Him;
their hearts will live for the age of the age.

All the prosperous of the earth ate and bowed down;
before Him all who descend into the earth will fall,
and my soul lives for Him.

He turned my soul back;
He guided me upon paths of righteousness
for His name’s sake.

For even if I walk in the midst of death’s shadow,
I will fear no evils, for Thou art with me;
Thy rod and Thy staff comforted me.

Thou didst prepare a table before me opposite those who afflict me;
Thou didst enrich my head with oil,
and Thy cup is intoxicating—how excellent!

Who is this King of glory?
The Lord, strong and powerful;
the Lord, powerful in war.

Do not remember the sins of my youth or my acts of ignorance;
according to Thy mercy, remember me Thyself,
for Thy kindness’ sake, Lord.

For He hid me in a tent in the day of my troubles;
He sheltered me in the hiding place of His tent;
He raised me upon a rock.

And now, behold, He raised my head above my enemies;
I went around and sacrificed in His tent a sacrifice of shouting;
I will sing and make music to the Lord.

Do not hand me over to the souls of those who afflict me,
for unjust witnesses rose against me,
and injustice lied to itself.

Wait for the Lord;
act courageously, and let your heart be strong,
and wait for the Lord.

Give them according to their works
and according to the wickedness of their practices;
give them according to the works of their hands;
repay their recompense to them.

The Lord is my helper and my protector;
in Him my heart hoped, and I was helped,
and my flesh blossomed anew;
from my own will I will thank Him.

A psalm of David, for the departure of the tent.
Bring to the Lord, sons of God;
bring to the Lord young rams;
bring to the Lord glory and honor.

The Lord’s voice is over the waters;
the God of glory thundered;
the Lord is over many waters.

The voice of the Lord, who makes deer ready;
and He will uncover forests;
in His temple everyone speaks glory.

Incline Thine ear to me;
hasten to bring me out;
be for me a protecting God
and a house of refuge to save me.

I will exult and rejoice in Thy mercy,
because Thou didst look upon my humiliation;
Thou didst save my soul from constraints

Have mercy on me, Lord, for I am afflicted;
my eye was troubled with anger,
my soul and my belly too.

For I heard the reproach of many dwelling all around;
as they gathered together against me,
they planned to take my soul.

My seasons are in Thy hands;
rescue me from the hand of my enemies
and from those who pursue me.

Do not become like a horse and mule that have no understanding;
with bridle and muzzle tighten their jaws—
those that do not approach you.

Of David.
Exult in the Lord, righteous ones;
praise is fitting for the upright.

The Lord scatters the counsels of nations;
He nullifies the plans of peoples
and nullifies the counsels of rulers.

Of David.
Judge, Lord, those who wrong me;
make war on those who make war on me.

Let a trap they do not know come upon them;
let the snare they hid catch them,
and into that trap they will fall.

But when they troubled me, I put on sackcloth
and humbled my soul with fasting;
and my prayer will return to my bosom.

But against me they rejoiced and gathered;
scourges gathered against me, and I did not know;
they were torn apart and felt no remorse.

May those who desire my righteousness exult and rejoice;
let them always say, “May the Lord be magnified”—
those who desire His servant’s peace.

He devised lawlessness upon his bed;
he stood by every way that was not good,
and he was not offended by wickedness.

Thy righteousness is like mountains of God;
Thy judgments are a great deep.
Thou wilt save humans and beasts, Lord.

Submit to the Lord and beseech Him;
do not be provoked to envy by one prospering in his way,
by a person committing lawless deeds.

For sinners will perish;
the Lord’s enemies, as soon as they are glorified and exalted,
vanished away like smoke—they vanished.

Wait for the Lord and keep His way;
He will exalt you to inherit the land;
you will see when sinners are destroyed.

The Lord will help them and rescue them;
He will remove them from sinners
and save them, because they have hoped in Him.

Those seeking my soul used violence;
those seeking evils for me spoke vain things
and meditated on deceptions all day long.

Indeed a person passes through as an image;
yet they are troubled in vain.
He stores treasure and does not know for whom he will gather it.

I proclaimed good news of righteousness in a great assembly;
behold, I will certainly not restrain my lips;
Lord, Thou knowest.

I did not hide Thy righteousness in my heart;
I spoke of Thy truth and Thy salvation.
I did not hide Thy mercy and Thy truth from a great congregation.

May all seeking Thee exult and rejoice in Thee, Lord;
let those loving Thy salvation always say,
“May the Lord be magnified!”

But I am poor and needy;
the Lord will care for me.
Thou art my helper and defender;
my God, do not delay.

If someone entered to see me, he spoke vainly;
his heart gathered lawlessness for himself;
he went outside and spoke.

My soul was troubled within me;
therefore I will remember Thee from the land of Jordan
and Hermoniim, from a small mountain.

A psalm of David.
Judge me, God, and judge my case against an unholy nation;
rescue me from an unjust and deceitful person.

Send out Thy light and Thy truth;
they guided me and brought me to Thy holy mountain
and to Thy dwellings.

Then I will go in to God’s altar,
to God who gladdens my youth;
I will thank Thee with the lyre, God, my God.

God, with our ears we heard;
our fathers announced to us
the work Thou didst in their days, in ancient days.

My heart poured forth a good word;
I speak my works to the king;
my tongue is the reed of a swiftly writing scribe.

Fair in beauty beyond the sons of men,
grace was poured upon your lips;
therefore God blessed you for ever.

and stretch forth, prosper and reign
for the sake of truth and meekness and righteousness;
your right hand will guide you wondrously.

You loved righteousness and hated lawlessness;
therefore God, your God, anointed you
with the oil of exultation beyond your companions.

Daughters of kings are in your honor;
the queen stood at your right in clothing woven with gold,
arrayed in varied embroidery.

They will remember your name in every generation;
therefore peoples will thank you
for ever and for age upon age.

The rulers of peoples gathered with Abraham’s God;
for the mighty of the earth belong to God;
they were greatly exalted.

Just as we heard, so we saw
in the city of the Lord of powers, in our God’s city;
God founded her for ever. Diapsalma.

According to Thy name, God,
so also Thy praise reaches the earth’s limits;
Thy right hand is full of righteousness.

For this is God, our God
for ever and for age upon age;
He will shepherd us through the ages.

Their tombs are their houses for ever,
their dwellings from generation to generation;
they invoked their names upon their lands.

our God, and He will not keep silent;
fire will burn before Him,
and around Him is a mighty tempest.

“Hear, My people, and I will speak unto you;
Israel, I testify unto you.
I am God, your God.

These things you did, and I kept silent;
you conceived the lawless thought that I would be like you.
I will rebuke you and set it before your face.

Then Thou wilt delight in a sacrifice of righteousness,
an offering and burnt offerings;
then they will bring calves upon Thine altar.

Therefore God will pull you down completely;
may He pluck you out and remove you from your dwelling,
and your root from the land of the living. Diapsalma.

But I am like a fruitful olive tree in God’s house;
I hoped in God’s mercy
for ever and for age upon age.

A fool said in his heart, “There is no God.”
They became corrupt and abominable in lawless deeds;
there is no one doing good.

For outsiders rose against me,
and powerful men sought my soul;
they did not set God before themselves. Diapsalma.

But Thou, God, wilt bring them down into a well of corruption;
men of bloodshed and deceit shall certainly not live out half their days.
But I will hope in Thee, Lord.

They will sojourn and conceal themselves;
they will watch my heel,
just as they waited for my soul.

He sent from heaven and saved me;
He gave those trampling me over to reproach. Diapsalma.
God sent His mercy and His truth

For behold, they hunted my soul;
powerful men attacked me.
Neither my lawlessness nor my sin, Lord—

And Thou, Lord, God of powers, God of Israel,
attend to visiting all the nations;
have no compassion on any who work lawlessness. Diapsalma.

Behold, they will speak out with their mouths,
and a sword is on their lips;
for who has heard?

Do not kill them, lest they forget my people;
scatter them by Thy power and bring them down,
Lord, my defender.

The sin of their mouth, the word of their lips—
let them be caught in their arrogance;
and from curse and falsehood consummations will be announced

My helper, I will make music unto Thee,
for Thou, God, art my supporter,
my God, my mercy.

Gilead is Mine, and Manasseh is Mine;
Ephraim is the strengthening of My head;
Judah is My king.

Moab is the basin of My hope;
upon Idumea I will extend My sandal;
foreigners were subjected to Me.”

Nevertheless they planned to reject my honor;
they ran in falsehood;
they blessed with their mouths but cursed with their hearts. Diapsalma.

Hope in Him, all the assembly of the people;
pour out your hearts before Him.
God is our helper. Diapsalma.

Nevertheless the sons of men are vain;
the sons of men are false upon scales for doing injustice,
they themselves together from vanity.

But the king will rejoice in God;
everyone swearing by Him will be praised,
for the mouth of those speaking unjust things was stopped.

They strengthened an evil word for themselves;
they discussed concealing traps;
they said, “Who will see them?”

They searched out lawless deeds;
they failed while searching with a search.
A human being will approach, and a deep heart,

Blessed is the one Thou didst choose and take to Thyself;
he will dwell in Thy courts.
We will be filled with the good things of Thy house;
holy is Thy sanctuary, wondrous in righteousness.

Thou didst visit the earth and make it drunk;
Thou didst multiply its enrichment.
God’s river was filled with water;
Thou didst prepare their food, for thus is Thy preparation.

Make its furrows drunk;
multiply its produce;
in its drops it will rejoice as it sprouts.

The rams of the sheep clothed themselves,
and the valleys will abound in grain;
they will cry out, for indeed they will sing hymns.

He who turns the sea into dry land;
through a river they will pass on foot.
There we will rejoice in Him,

who rules the age by His power;
His eyes look upon the nations.
Let those provoking Him not exalt themselves within themselves. Diapsalma.

Thou madest human beings mount our heads;
we passed through fire and water,
and Thou broughtest us out to refreshment.

I will offer Thee marrow-rich whole burnt offerings,
with incense and rams;
I will prepare oxen with he-goats for Thee. Diapsalma.

As smoke vanishes, let them vanish;
as wax melts before fire,
so may sinners perish before God.

God’s chariot is ten-thousandfold,
thousands of flourishing ones;
the Lord is among them, in Sinai, in the holy place.

There is Benjamin, the younger, in ecstasy;
Judah’s rulers, their leaders,
Zebulun’s rulers, Naphtali’s rulers.

Give glory to God;
His magnificence is over Israel,
and His power in the clouds.

Wondrous is God among His holy ones;
the God of Israel will give power and strengthening to His people.
Blessed is God.

More numerous than the hairs on my head became those hating me without cause;
my enemies pursuing me unjustly became strong.
What I did not plunder, I was then repaying.

But I, in my prayer, turn toward Thee, Lord;
a time of favor, God, in the abundance of Thy mercy.
Hear me in the truth of Thy salvation.

Let no tempest of water drown me,
nor the depth swallow me;
let no well close its mouth over me.

My soul expected reproach and misery;
I waited for someone to grieve with me, but there was none,
for comforters, but found none.

For God will save Zion,
and Judea’s cities will be built;
they will dwell there and inherit it.

Let all who seek Thee exult and be glad in Thee;
let those who love Thy salvation always say,
“Let God be magnified!”

But I am poor and needy;
God, help me!
Thou art my helper and my rescuer;
Lord, do not delay!

Of David; of the sons of Jonadab and of those first taken captive.
God, in Thee I have hoped;
may I never be disgraced.

Upon Thee I was supported from the womb;
from my mother’s belly Thou art the One who shelters me.
My hymn is continually in Thee.

For I too will acknowledge unto Thee Thy truth with a musical instrument, God;
I will sing unto Thee with a lyre,
Holy One of Israel.

And he will live, and some of Arabia’s gold will be given to him;
and they will pray concerning him continually,
and bless him all day.

There will be a firm support in the land upon the mountain summits;
his fruit will be raised far above Lebanon,
and they will blossom from the city like the earth’s grass.

Let his name be blessed through the ages;
before the sun his name will endure.
And all the tribes of the earth will be blessed in him;
all nations will call him blessed.

And blessed be His glorious name for the age and for the age of the age;
and the whole earth will be filled with His glory.
May it be! May it be!

Remember Thy congregation, which Thou didst acquire from the beginning;
Thou didst redeem the rod of Thine inheritance,
this Mount Zion, where Thou didst encamp.

We did not see our signs;
there is no prophet any longer,
and he will know us no longer.

The earth and all who inhabit it melted;
I established its pillars.
Diapsalma.

For in the Lord’s hand is a cup
of unmixed wine, full of mixture;
and He tilted from this into that,
but its dregs were not emptied out;
all the earth’s sinners will drink.

All those without understanding in heart were troubled;
they slept their sleep,
and all the men of wealth found nothing with their hands.

In the day of my affliction I sought God,
with my hands at night before Him, and I was not deceived;
my soul refused to be comforted.

I remembered God and was glad;
I spoke at length, and my spirit lost heart.
Diapsalma.

The waters saw Thee, God;
the waters saw Thee and feared,
and the depths were troubled—a multitude of sounding waters.

Thy thunder’s voice was in the wheel;
Thy flashes of lightning shone upon the inhabited world;
the earth shook and became trembling.

Of understanding. Of Asaph.
Attend, my people, to my law;
bend your ear to the words of my mouth.

so that another generation might know,
sons who will be born;
and they will rise and announce it to their sons,

Therefore the Lord heard and delayed;
and fire was kindled in Jacob,
and wrath rose against Israel,

He made a road for His wrath;
He did not spare their souls from death,
and confined their cattle to death,

from behind the ewes giving birth He took him,
to shepherd Jacob His people
and Israel His inheritance.

A psalm for Asaph.
God, nations entered Thine inheritance;
they defiled Thy holy temple;
they made Jerusalem into a fruit-watchman’s hut.

Do not remember our ancient acts of lawlessness;
let Thy compassions swiftly reach us first,
for we became very poor.

Let the groaning of those in bonds enter before Thee;
according to the greatness of Thine arm,
preserve the sons of those put to death.

But we, Thy people and the sheep of Thy pasture,
will give Thee thanks for ever;
from generation to generation we will proclaim Thy praise.

Thou who shepherdest Israel, pay attention,
Thou who guidest Joseph like sheep;
Thou who sittest upon the cherubim, appear.

Lord, God of powers, turn us back;
make Thy face shine, and we shall be saved.
Diapsalma.

God of powers, turn back now;
look from heaven and see,
and visit this vine,

He established it as a testimony in Joseph,
when he went out from the land of Egypt;
a language he did not know, he heard.

In affliction you called on Me, and I delivered you;
I heard you in the hidden place of the storm;
I tested you at the water of contention.
Diapsalma.

They did not know or understand;
they pass through darkness;
all the foundations of the earth will be shaken.

For Asshur too came alongside them;
they became a support for the sons of Lot.
Diapsalma.

Blessed are those who dwell in Thy house;
they will praise Thee for ages of ages.
Diapsalma.

Lord, God of powers, hear my prayer;
give ear, God of Jacob.
Diapsalma.

For one day in Thy courts is better than thousands;
I chose to be cast aside in the house of God
rather than dwell in the tents of sinners.

For the Lord God loves mercy and truth;
He will give grace and glory;
the Lord will not deprive those who walk in innocence of good things.

Thou forgavest Thy people their acts of lawlessness;
Thou didst cover all their sins.
Diapsalma.

Guard my soul, for I am holy;
save Thy servant, my God,
who hopes in Thee.

Guide me in Thy way, Lord,
and I will walk in Thy truth;
let my heart rejoice to fear Thy name.

God, lawless people rose up against me,
and an assembly of strong men sought my soul;
they did not set Thee before them.

Look upon me and have mercy on me;
give Thy might to Thy servant
and save the son of Thy maidservant.

“Mother Zion,” a man will say,
and a man was born in her;
and the Most High Himself founded her.

I was counted with those descending into a pit;
I became like a person without help,
free among the dead,

Thou didst remove my acquaintances far from me;
they made me an abomination to themselves.
I was handed over and did not go out.

My eyes grew weak from poverty.
I cried unto Thee, Lord, all day;
I spread my hands toward Thee:

Then Thou spakest in a vision to Thy holy ones and saidst:
“I placed help upon a powerful man;
I raised a chosen one from My people.

and like the moon, established for ever;
and the witness in heaven is faithful.”
Diapsalma.

Thou didst shorten the days of his time;
Thou didst pour shame over him.
Diapsalma.

For all our days failed,
and in Thine anger we failed;
I pondered our years like a spider.

With His shoulders He will overshadow you,
and under His wings you will hope;
His truth will surround you with a weapon.

He will call upon Me, and I will hear him;
I am with him in affliction,
and I will take him out and glorify him.

From the voices of many waters,
wondrous are the sea’s surges;
wondrous on high is the Lord.

Thy testimonies were made very sure;
sanctity befits Thy house, Lord,
for length of days.

A psalm of David, for the fourth day of the week.
The God of vengeance is the Lord;
the God of vengeance spoke openly.

A praise of a song, of David.
Come, let us exult in the Lord;
let us shout to God our Savior.

When the house was being built after the captivity; a song of David.
Sing to the Lord a new song;
sing to the Lord, all the earth.

Of David, when his land is being established.
The Lord has become King! Let the earth exult;
let many islands rejoice.

You who love the Lord, hate evil!
The Lord guards the souls of His holy ones;
He will rescue them from the hand of sinners.

The King’s honor loves judgment.
Thou didst prepare uprightness;
judgment and righteousness in Jacob Thou hast done.

Lord our God, Thou heardest them;
God, Thou wast gracious to them
and tookest vengeance for all their practices.

Know that the Lord—He is God.
He made us, and not we;
His people and the sheep of His pasture.

Do not turn Thy face away from me.
On whatever day I am afflicted, incline Thine ear to me;
on whatever day I call upon Thee, hear me quickly.

They will perish, but Thou wilt remain;
all will grow old like a garment.
Like a cloak Thou wilt change them, and they will be changed.

He makes grass spring up for livestock
and green plants for the service of humans,
to bring bread out of the earth;

How great Thy works have become, Lord!
Thou madest all things in wisdom;
the earth was filled with Thy possession.

Here is the sea, great and spacious;
there are creeping things without number,
living creatures small with great.

Hallelujah.
Give thanks to the Lord and call upon His name;
announce His works among the nations.

Hallelujah.
Give thanks to the Lord, for He is good;
His mercy is for ever.

Our fathers in Egypt did not understand Thy wonders;
they did not remember the abundance of Thy mercy
and provoked Thee while going up in the Red Sea.

and shed innocent blood,
the blood of their sons and daughters whom they sacrificed to Canaan’s carved images;
the land was murdered with blood,

Hallelujah.
Give thanks to the Lord, for He is good;
His mercy is for ever.

They rise as far as the heavens
and descend as far as the deeps;
their soul melted in evils.

Gilead is Mine, and Manasseh is Mine;
Ephraim is the support of My head;
Judah is My king.

Moab is the cauldron of My hope;
over Idumea I will extend My sandal;
foreign peoples were subjected to Me.

He clothed himself in a curse like a garment;
it entered his innards like water
and his bones like oil.

They will curse, but Thou wilt bless;
let those rising against me be ashamed,
but Thy servant will rejoice.

With you is rule on the day of your power,
in the splendors of the holy ones;
from the womb, before the morning star, I begot you.

He sent redemption to His people;
He commanded His covenant for ever;
holy and fearsome is His name.

The beginning of wisdom is the fear of the Lord;
good understanding belongs to all who practice it.
His praise remains for an age of an age.

Hallelujah!
Blessed is the man who fears the Lord;
he will greatly delight in His commandments.

He scattered gifts; he gave to the poor.
His righteousness remains for an age of an age;
his horn will be raised in glory.

A sinner will see and be angry;
he will gnash his teeth and waste away;
the desire of sinners will perish.

Hallelujah!
Praise the Lord, servants;
praise the name of the Lord.

But our God is in heaven above;
in the heavens and on the earth
He has done everything He wished.

They have hands and will not feel;
feet, and will not walk;
they will not sound with their throat.

The Lord remembered us and blessed us;
He blessed the house of Israel;
He blessed the house of Aaron.

The pangs of death surrounded me;
the dangers of Hades found me;
I found affliction and pain.

for He rescued my soul from death,
my eyes from tears,
and my feet from slipping.

O Lord, I am Thy slave;
I am Thy slave and the son of Thy slave woman.
Thou hast torn apart my bonds.

Hallelujah.
Praise the Lord, all nations;
laud Him, all peoples,

Three: Gimal.
Recompense Thy servant;
I will live and keep Thy words.

Four: Delth.
My soul clung to the ground;
give me life according to Thy word.

Eight: Ēth.
Thou art my portion, Lord;
I said that I would keep Thy law.

Ten: Iōth.
Thy hands made me and formed me;
give me understanding, and I will learn Thy commandments.

From Thy commandments I gained understanding;
therefore I hated every way of injustice,
for Thou didst instruct me.

Sixteen: Ain.
I did judgment and righteousness;
do not hand me over to those who wrong me.

Seventeen: Phē.
Thy testimonies are wonderful;
therefore my soul searched them out.

Nineteen: Kōph.
I cried with my whole heart; hear me, Lord;
I will seek Thine ordinances.

Twenty-two: Thau.
Let my supplication draw near before Thee, Lord;
give me understanding according to Thy saying.

for there the tribes went up,
the tribes of the Lord—a testimony for Israel—
to give thanks to the Lord’s name.

Our soul was rescued like a little bird
from the trap of hunters;
the trap was shattered, and we were rescued.

A song of the ascents.
Those trusting in the Lord are like Mount Zion;
the one dwelling in Jerusalem will never be shaken.

And passersby have not said,
“The Lord’s blessing be upon you;
we have blessed you in the Lord’s name.”

Lord, hear my voice;
let Thine ears be attentive
to the voice of my petition.

My soul hoped in the Lord
from the morning watch until night;
from the morning watch let Israel hope in the Lord.

Like ointment upon the head,
descending upon the beard, Aaron’s beard,
descending upon the border of his garment;

Hallelujah!
Praise the Lord’s name;
praise the Lord, slaves,

He brings clouds up from the earth’s extremity;
He made lightning for rain;
He brings winds out of His treasuries.

They have ears but will not listen;
they have noses but will not smell;
they have hands but will not touch;
they have feet but will not walk;
they will not sound in their throat,
for there is no breath in their mouth.

Hallelujah!
Give thanks to the Lord, for He is kind;
for His mercy is for ever.

To Him who led His people through the wilderness;
for His mercy is for ever.
To Him who brought water out of a sheer rock;
for His mercy is for ever.

Give thanks to the God of heaven;
for His mercy is for ever.
Give thanks to the Lord of lords;
for His mercy is for ever.

May my tongue cling to my throat
if I do not remember you,
if I do not set Jerusalem first at the beginning of my gladness.

If I walk amid affliction, Thou wilt keep me alive;
against my enemies’ anger Thou didst stretch out Thy hand,
and Thy right hand saved me.

The Lord will repay on my behalf.
Lord, Thy mercy is for ever;
do not neglect the works of Thy hands.

For darkness will not be dark from Thee,
and night will be lit up like day;
as its darkness, so also its light.

I will thank Thee, for I was made fearfully wonderful;
wondrous are Thy works,
and my soul knows very well.

Thine eyes saw my unworked substance,
and in Thy book all will be written;
they will be formed over days, and none among them.

Guard me, Lord, from a sinner’s hand;
rescue me from unjust people,
those who devised to trip my steps.

The proud hid a trap for me
and stretched cords, traps for my feet;
along the path they set a stumbling block for me. Diapsalma.

Coals will fall upon them;
in fire Thou wilt cast them down;
in miseries they will certainly not withstand.

I cried unto Thee, Lord;
I said, Thou art my hope,
my portion in the land of the living.

I remembered ancient days
and meditated on all Thy works;
I was pondering the works of Thy hands.

Send out Thy hand from on high;
take me out and rescue me from many waters,
from the hand of foreigners.

Their storehouses full, pouring forth from this to that;
their sheep bearing many young,
multiplying in their outgoing places.

Their oxen fat;
there is no collapse of a fence and no passage out,
nor any cry in their squares.

The Lord raises up those broken down;
the Lord makes the blind wise;
the Lord loves the righteous.

The Lord guards the newcomers;
He will take up the orphan and widow,
and He will obliterate the way of sinners.

Hallelujah. Of Haggai and Zechariah.
Praise the Lord, for a psalm is good;
may praise be pleasing to our God.

Hallelujah. Of Haggai and Zechariah.
Commend the Lord, Jerusalem;
praise your God, Zion.

Hallelujah. Of Haggai and Zechariah.
Praise the Lord from the heavens;
praise Him in the highest places.

Let them praise the Lord’s name,
for He spoke, and they came to be;
He commanded, and they were created.

Hallelujah.
Praise God among His holy ones;
praise Him in the firmament of His power.
